# Datris Platform - Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Set EITHER ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or OPENAI_API_KEY. vault-init.sh seeds the AI
# primary, codegen, and embedding secrets based on which key you provided.
# Web search (Configuration → AI Providers) reuses the same keys — no
# separate seeding required.
#
# This file is "live": when you save changes in the AI Configuration UI, the
# server mirrors ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY, and the *_MODEL overrides
# back to this file so they survive `docker compose down && up`. Only those
# AI keys are touched — comments, ordering, and unrelated values are
# preserved. Single-tenant only (multi-tenant deployments don't share .env).
#
# HIGHLY RECOMMENDED: Anthropic with the latest coding model for CodeGen.
# Tap script generation, AI DQ rules, AI transformations, and NL→SQL all
# depend heavily on the model's coding ability — Claude produces dramatically
# better results than smaller/cheaper models.
#
# HIGHLY RECOMMENDED for embeddings: OpenAI text-embedding-3-small for the
# most reliable, low-cost path — works on any host. For a fully-local
# zero-cost setup, Ollama with bge-m3 is a strong open-source alternative.
# See EMBEDDING_PROVIDER below to mix-and-match (e.g. Claude for chat plus
# OpenAI for embeddings when the bundled embedder is too heavy for your host).
#
# Anthropic path: ai-primary and codegen use Claude. Embedding falls back to
# the bundled TEI sidecar serving bge-m3 (a strong open-source embedding
# model, 1024 dimensions) — no OpenAI key needed for vector destinations.
#
# OpenAI path: all three secrets use OpenAI from the same key.

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Optional explicit chat-provider override. Pin a choice when both keys are
# present, or when a stray shell env var (e.g. a global OPENAI_API_KEY in
# your shell rc) would otherwise leak in and silently flip the default on
# every rebuild. When unset, vault-init picks whichever key is present
# (OpenAI wins ties, preserving the historical default).
# AI_PROVIDER=anthropic

# Optional model overrides (defaults shown)
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5.5
# CODEGEN_MODEL=claude-opus-4-7   # or gpt-5.5 if using OpenAI

# Model the Assistant falls back to when Anthropic returns sustained
# `overloaded_error` for an Opus call (after 2 retries at 1s + 3s backoff).
# Heavy Opus requests (many tools + extended thinking + streaming) sit in
# Anthropic's most-load-shed lane, so a one-shot downgrade to Sonnet for
# the current request keeps the conversation moving instead of surfacing
# the error. The UI shows a small inline notice when the fallback fires.
# Only consulted when the current model is an Anthropic Opus variant —
# OpenAI-only and other-provider deployments can ignore this entirely.
# Bump this when a newer Sonnet ships so the fallback stays current
# without a recompile.
# ANTHROPIC_OVERLOAD_FALLBACK_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6

# Optional embedding provider override (decoupled from AI_PROVIDER).
# By default the embedding slot follows AI_PROVIDER: anthropic→bundled TEI
# (bge-m3, 1024-dim), openai→OpenAI text-embedding-3-small (1536-dim).
# Set EMBEDDING_PROVIDER to mix-and-match — e.g. Anthropic for chat/codegen
# and OpenAI for embedding when you don't want to run the bundled TEI sidecar.
# Valid values: openai, tei, ollama. EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=openai requires
# OPENAI_API_KEY. EMBEDDING_MODEL overrides the default model for the chosen
# provider; EMBEDDING_ENDPOINT overrides the URL for tei/ollama only.
# EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=openai
# EMBEDDING_MODEL=text-embedding-3-small
# EMBEDDING_ENDPOINT=

# Auth / multi-tenancy toggles (defaults shown — single-tenant OSS).
# Flip USE_USER_AUTH=true to enable username/password login + admin gating
# on the Configuration tab. USE_API_KEYS=true enables per-tenant API-key
# gating on the REST/MCP API. MULTI_TENANT=true switches to per-tenant
# database isolation (intended for hosted/managed deployments).
# See https://docs.datris.ai/user-auth for the full setup walkthrough.
# USE_USER_AUTH=false
# USE_API_KEYS=false
# MULTI_TENANT=false

# API keys for accessing Datris (REST API or via the bundled MCP server) are
# managed in the Configuration UI's Secrets tab — entries in `oss/api-keys`
# under USE_API_KEYS=true, and per-tenant under MULTI_TENANT=true. There is
# no env var here for them. Agents (Claude Desktop, Cursor, etc.) and external
# REST clients send their own `x-api-key` header per request; mcp-server
# forwards whatever the connecting agent provides.

# Optional bundled Ollama service model (only used if you uncomment the
# `ollama` service in docker-compose.yml — disabled by default). This is the
# model Ollama pulls on first start; pick anything available at
# https://ollama.com/library. Once enabled, you can point AI Primary or
# CodeGen at it via the Configuration tab.
# OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen2.5:14b-instruct
